                                "sense_id": "239e2778-0d53-375b-a0dd-e069e358ed4f",
                                "text": "The kind of identity that the Ricoeurian self has is not like the nonpersonal entities that perdure simply as in some significant sense “selfsame.” Rather, the self's identity is constituted by an inextricable tie between a selfsameness and a selfhood or ipseity."
